```sql
-- DDL: define structure (auto-commits)
CREATE TABLE products (id INT PRIMARY KEY, name VARCHAR(80));

-- DML: change data (transactional)
INSERT INTO products VALUES (1, 'Phone');
UPDATE products SET name = 'Smartphone' WHERE id = 1;

-- DQL: read data
SELECT id, name FROM products;
```

Sample output (SELECT):

| id | name |
|---|---|
| 1 | Smartphone |

```sql
BEGIN;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = 1;
SAVEPOINT after_debit;                       -- marker

UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 2;
-- something wrong with the credit? undo only the credit:
ROLLBACK TO after_debit;

UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = 3;
COMMIT;   -- debit + credit-to-3 become permanent together
```

*`SAVEPOINT` enables partial rollback; `COMMIT` finalizes the whole transaction.*
